@@ -11,4 +11,12 @@ refers to. It throws an `Error` when the pointer is invalid (it must be empty or
 must be followed by `0` or `1`) or when it does not resolve: missing member, array index out of range,
 `-`, a non-canonical index such as `01`, or a step into a primitive. Only own members are resolved.
 
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) and returns the result as a new value; the
+input is never mutated. It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid or an operation fails (including a
+failed `test`); the patch is atomic, so no partial result is returned. `test` compares values by deep
+equality, ignoring member order.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
